{
  "about": "Performance budget of the storefront audit (setup/audit/lighthouse.mjs). Each page fails the lighthouse workflow when the median of its runs is worse than its reference value moved by the tolerance of the metric and preset: lower for a score, higher for a time, a shift, a weight or a request count. The reference is a measure of the workflow itself, written here by hand with its date and commit: it is raised when an improvement is acquired, never rewritten from the last run.",
  "toleranceBasis": "2026-11-17, four measures of the same served storefront (core commits 155cbe071, af9ed4f3b, a496c7463 and 19201dc07, which differ only in the workflow, Flexy dev-main bf04b3b4d) on GitHub runners; the reference is their median. Desktop: performance moved by 3 points and FCP and LCP by 5 % at most, except the LCP of the product page, which is its lazily loaded first gallery image and arrives early or late (0.83 to 1.49 s). Mobile, simulated by Lighthouse on a slow 4G, moved by steps: up to 16 points of performance, 54 % of FCP and 92 % of LCP, so its times only catch a gross regression. Accessibility, best practices, SEO, CLS, TBT, weight (under 0.2 %) and requests did not move on either preset: they hold the tight thresholds.",
